    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374-a11">

                <pb facs="0750" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg640"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    297.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Azpiroz to Mr.
                            Ryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: The President of the Republic
                    having approved the arrangement entered into between Your Excellency and Señor
                    Lie. Don Ignacio Mariscal, secretary of foreign affairs, relative to the
                    indemnification of Deputy Sheriff Shadrack White with $7,000, in United States
                    gold coin, for the injuries sustained by him through the wound he received
                    during the unfortunate incident of March 3, 1888, at Eagle Pass, I have the
                    honor to transmit to Your Excellency a draft for the amount aforestated, drawn
                    by the Bank of London and Mexico against the Bank of British North America, of
                    New York, and by me indorsed to Your Excellency.</p>
                <p>I pray that Your Excellency may be pleased to acknowledge receipt of said draft;
                    and I embrace this occasion, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Azpiroz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
